se},{"w":"a","s":44.69,"e":44.713,"line":"c1","accent":false,"brk":false},{"w":"day?","s":44.748,"e":44.994,"line":"c1","accent":false,"brk":false},{"w":"Head","s":45.054,"e":45.216,"line":"c1","accent":false,"brk":true},{"w":"to","s":45.251,"e":45.321,"line":"c1","accent":false,"brk":false},{"w":"Teyro.","s":45.367,"e":46.041,"line":"c1","accent":true,"brk":false}],"lines":[{"id":"h1","start":0.12,"end":5.095,"text":"You can now use Claude Code to rewrite Claude Code itself, and someone's already running Doom inside it."},{"id":"i1","start":5.195,"end":10.743,"text":"Last week, Anthropic shipped mods, a way to change almost everything in it, from the spinner to your prompts."},{"id":"i2","start":10.843,"end":16.784,"text":"Under the hood, it runs on events. Sending a prompt is one. Running a tool is one. Even drawing the spinner is one."},{"id":"i3","start":16.884,"end":23.413,"text":"A mod is a bit of TypeScript that sits on those events, and it can watch one, change it, or answer it, so the original never runs."},{"id":"i4","start":23.513,"end":30.232,"text":"Anthropic's Blast Radius mod catches a risky delete and shows what it would wipe. Token Weather draws a forecast of your context."},{"id":"i5","start":30.332,"end":35.638,"text":"You don't even have to write them. Ask Claude for one that shows your Git branch, and it loads when the turn ends."},{"id":"i6","start":35.738,"end":40.086,"text":"The catch? Mods aren't sandboxed, so a bad one could read your API keys."},{"id":"i7","start":40.186,"end":42.953,"text":"And Claude Code's own diff view is already a mod."},{"id":"c1","start":43.053,"end":45.826,"text":"Want to learn Claude Code, one lesson a day? Head to Teyro."}],"lip":{"amp":[0,0,0,0,0.002,0.003,1,1,0.915,0.294,1,1,1,1,0.966,0.975,1,0.935,0.82,1,1,1,1,0.688,0.308,0.241,0.295,0.956,1,1,1,0.566,0.214,0.039,0.372,0.529,1,1,1,1,1,0.852,0.556,0.424,0.662,1,1,1,1,1,1,0.593,1,1,1,0.909,0.103,0.03,0.498,0.285,0.933,1,1,1,0.389,0.175,0.456,0.42,1,1,1,0.535,1,0